Codecov plus quotas plus remote stay qualified with fixture evidence (issue #507).

Codecov stays at most opt-in and is never required. No Codecov account
activation or upload wiring is used here: no codecov-action, no
CODECOV_TOKEN, no codecov upload step in workflows, tools, or CLI.
The first-party comment rendered from the Bazel-owned gate verdict is
the adopted PR surface (seed cell owns the PR comment; arm64 plus musl
plus macos plus windows cells report to their job
summaries). Consumer coverage stays per-cell with no union and Codecov
opt-in only through reusable-consumer.yml.

Free-tier qualification covers only the services actually used:
standard GitHub-hosted runners are free for public repositories
(ubuntu-latest, ubuntu-24.04-arm, macos-14, windows-latest; no
self-hosted, no larger, no unpinned macos-latest). actions/cache disk
cache is 10 GB per repository; artifact storage is 500 MB. Larger
runners are always charged.

Remote stays local-only with the else branch taken: hermeticity is
designed and locally sandbox-tested (aquery action shape plus
execution-log cache hits) but remote behavior remains unverified, with
no remote cache or executor wired (--remote_cache, --remote_executor,
--bes_backend appear nowhere in owned config or workflows). No
remote-cache correctness or remotely-executable claim is made in docs;
platform qualification beyond the seed host stays owned under issue
#298. Local cache evidence stays wired via quality_cache_aquery.sh
(cache hit) plus examples_laziness_runtime.sh.

Seed only for platform plus consumer plus release evidence; no
Supported claim.
